KZ3 patch 4028 (network pass 47; ENHANCEMENT, opt-in, default off): the DSU (cemuhook) gyro client.
pad_dsu.h (CRC32, request, strict parser, SIXAXIS word conversion), pad_dsu_io.h (one UDP socket bound to 127.0.0.1 and
connect()ed to 127.0.0.1:<port>, polled from the pad poll, no thread). keybinds.ini [motion] dsu_port = off|<port
1024..65535> (bridge "dsu" / "dsu <off|port>", the Layout and Prompts page's row); KZ3_DSU_PORT overrides for tests.
While samples arrive they replace port 0's SIXAXIS words (the words the game's zoomed motion aim reads) and set the
prompts' motion flag. Loopback only by construction; every byte from the server is checked before it is used.
(The crouch Hold/Toggle of the same decision needs no patch: the game has it, Options > Controller > Advanced > Crouch.)

